16 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Schematic illustration showing the production stage where induced pluripotent stem cells are engineered with a CAR construct, differentiated into CAR-NK cells, and release engineered extracellular vesicles. In the proposed action stage, CAR-positive vesicles bind tumor-associated antigens, undergo cellular uptake or membrane interaction, deliver cytotoxic cargo, induce apoptosis, and contribute to tumor-cell death.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating CAR-NK extracellular vesicle movement from blood vessels through stromal barriers into the tumor microenvironment. The vesicles interact with tumor cells through CAR-antigen recognition, stress-ligand interactions, death-receptor pathways, and CD16-mediated antibody-dependent mechanisms. These interactions may promote direct apoptosis and cytotoxic cargo delivery while also influencing local immune cells, including dendritic cells.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Infographic showing a multi-step engineering strategy for CAR-NK extracellular vesicles. Genomic engineering of iPSCs includes CRISPR/Cas9-mediated knockout and knock-in of functional modules. Differentiated iPSC-NK producer cells express engineered surface proteins and release vesicles. The final engineered vesicles may contain perforin, granzyme B, siRNA or miRNA, chemotherapeutic cargo such as cisplatin, and surface molecules including CAR, hnCD16, and membrane-bound IL-15.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Illustration showing the proposed targeting of lung tumors by iPSC-derived CAR-NK extracellular vesicles. Vesicles carrying cytotoxic proteins, miRNAs, cytokines, and surface targeting molecules penetrate toward tumor tissue, interact with tumor-associated antigens, and may deliver functional cargo. The diagram also depicts tumor-microenvironment remodeling, immunosuppressive factors, stromal barriers, and induction of tumor-cell apoptosis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
